<title>FRANCE: OECD details revision in 1996 forecasts.</title>
<headline>OECD details revision in 1996 forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Organisation for Economic Co-operation and Development gave the following revised growth forecasts in its world economic outlook, compared to those made in its last outlook in June.</p>
<p>			   1996     1997     1998</p>
<p> United States	 2.4	2.2	2.0</p>
<p> June 1996	     2.3	2.0	N/A</p>
<p> Japan		   3.6	1.6	3.7</p>
<p> June 1996	     2.2	2.4	N/A</p>
<p> Germany		 1.1	2.2	2.6</p>
<p> June 1996	     0.5	2.4	N/A</p>
<p> European Union	1.6	2.4	2.7</p>
<p> June 1996 *	   N/A	N/A	N/A</p>
<p> Total OECD	    2.4	2.4	2.7</p>
<p> June 1996	     2.1	2.5	N/A</p>
<p>* Note: Forecasts at the level of the 15-nation European Union were not given last year.</p>
</text>
